// §14 entry 7 -- a wire struct whose declared bit widths leave a partial
// trailing byte -> EXS-E0322.
//
// RESTATED against the §5.2 amendment (commit 4edb704, checker.md finding
// 13): fields in a `@transitus` type are **packed, alignment 1, always** --
// offset is the sum of the preceding widths, with no alignment padding ever
// inserted. The certified `DeModFrame` (`vendor/hydramesh-wire/`) is only
// readable that way: `cursus: u16:maior` sits at byte 15 directly after a
// `u24` at byte 12, no gap. Under that reading this fixture's ORIGINAL form
// -- `Capitulum` with its `reserva: u16:maior` field simply deleted, leaving
// `versio: u8` and `genus: u8` butted against `signum`/`longitudo` -- is a
// valid, packed 10-byte struct. There is no natural-alignment gap between
// whole-byte fields for the checker to call implicit, because §5.2 no
// longer has such a gap at all; that fixture **does not reject**, and §14's
// own text changed to say so ("was 'implicit padding' -- under §5.2's
// packed layout the only padding a field can imply is the bit-granularity
// kind, rules 2 and 4").
//
// So entry 7 now has to violate rule 4 directly: "Declared widths must sum
// to a whole number of bytes. A partial trailing byte is implicit padding,"
// applied at bit granularity rather than byte granularity. Below, a
// multi-byte field (`u16:maior`, byte-boundary-aligned: it starts at byte 0
// and rule 2's "must begin on a byte boundary" is satisfied), a whole-byte
// field (`u8`, starts at byte 2), and a trailing sub-byte field (`u4`,
// starts at byte 3) sum to 16 + 8 + 4 = 28 bits -- 3.5 bytes, not a whole
// number. The trailing `u4` is deliberately last and alone: every field
// before it already lands on a byte boundary, so this fixture violates rule
// 4 only, not rule 2, and is a clean single-rule case (unlike entry 21,
// which violates rule 4 with a pair of adjacent sub-byte fields --
// `u4`+`u3` -- and never has a multi-byte field to also satisfy rule 2
// against).
//
// DEFERRED: needs the @transitus layout checker, which needs the type
// checker (Stage 2). compiler/x86_64/ast/ and cst/ are both still empty;
// `exsc aedifica`, run directly against this file, exits 0 and reports
// nothing -- confirmed, not assumed (see this suite's report).

@transitus
publica structura Malum {
    numerus: u16:maior
    genus:   u8
    versio:  u4
}

// TEST: entry=7 shape=code expect-code=EXS-E0322 status=deferred needs=wire_layout_checker
